# stable-files - ampliseq's core tables, as paths under results/: what a run's
# record keeps the checksums of, a re-run compares, and selftest checks. A line
# may add how the file is read for its checksum, as lib/outputs.sh says.
#
# Chosen by running its fixture jobs twice, then at another CPU count, as
# docs/migration.md's phase 6 notes record. Left out, because they vary from
# run to run with a known cause: the placement trees in pplace/, whose ASVs
# placed on one edge come in an order EPA-NG's threads decide, and whose
# placements themselves can differ from run to run; the BIOM files, which hold
# the time they were written; and the reports, PDFs and logs. Within tables:
# Faith's PD, measured on that tree. DADA2's bootstrap confidences are compared:
# DADA2_TAXONOMY runs in gnoto-dada2, whose ties break the same way every run.
dada2/ASV_table.tsv
dada2/ASV_seqs.fasta
dada2/ASV_tax.user.tsv
dada2/ASV_tax_species.user.tsv
dada2/DADA2_table.tsv
dada2/DADA2_stats.tsv
asv_length_filter/ASV_table.len.tsv
asv_length_filter/stats.len.tsv
barrnap/summary.tsv
abundance_tables/*.tsv
alpha_diversity.tsv drop faith
feature_table/feature-table.tsv
feature_table/feature-sequences.fasta
overall_summary.tsv
